chapter('grignard','RMgX strongly nucleophilic/basic carbon reagent છે. Carbonyl addition, ester double addition અને CO₂ carboxylation અલગ pathways છે; protic groups reagent quench કરી શકે છે.','R attacks C=O; work-up supplies the O–H proton.','Gilman reagents favor many conjugate additions; an ordinary uncatalyzed Grignard commonly gives 1,2-addition to an enone.',[grignard1,grignard2,grignard3],'Why is dry solvent needed before Grignard addition?','Protic water consumes the organomagnesium reagent',['Water makes the carbon infinitely more nucleophilic','Grignards are always stable in acid','Water is the essential hydride source'],'https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/19-7-nucleophilic-addition-of-hydride-and-grignard-reagents-alcohol-formation')
