chapter('gilman','Gilman reagent R₂CuLi organocuprate છે. Conjugate addition અને acyl-chloride-to-ketone conversion તેની useful selectivities છે; universal direct carbanion model આખી metal chemistry સમજાવતું નથી.','Cu: conjugate carbon delivery, keep the carbonyl.','RMgX/RLi are harder and more basic; Cu reagents often give different selectivity.',[gilman1,gilman2],'Where does a standard cuprate conjugate addition form the new C–C bond?','At the enone β-carbon',['At oxygen in every case','Only at aromatic nitrogen','At an already saturated remote carbon'])
chapter('rli','RLi organolithium compound માં C–Li bond strongly polarized છે. Strong basicity અને strong nucleophilicity બંને છે; deprotonation, metal–halogen exchange અને carbonyl addition વચ્ચે competition વિચારવી પડે છે.','RLi: ask “acidic H?” before “where will it add?”.','Organocuprates are softer; RLi can readily deprotonate substrates that a milder reagent leaves intact.',[pathway('rli-ketone','Organolithium addition to ketone','Propanone','CC(C)=O','1. PhLi, dry ether/THF; 2. H₃O⁺','2-Phenylpropan-2-ol','CC(O)(C)c1ccccc1','Phenyl lithium ketone પર phenyl carbon deliver કરે છે. Alkoxide ને work-up માં proton મળે છે; product tertiary alcohol છે.',org_steps,'Strongly polarized C–Li bonding gives a reactive carbon nucleophile; aggregation and solvent affect behavior.','No stereocenter because two methyl groups are identical.','An acidic proton can cause deprotonation instead of the desired addition.')],'Which competing reaction must be checked with RLi?','Deprotonation of an acidic substrate proton',['Only electrophilic aromatic chlorination','Mandatory epoxide formation','Universal 1,4-addition regardless of substrate'])

def protecting_path(id,title,start,smi,conditions,product,psmi,gu,mech,why,trap):
    return pathway(id,title,start,smi,conditions,product,psmi,gu,mech,why,'Protection ordinarily preserves pre-existing stereogenic carbon centers unless the conditions cause a separate reaction.',trap)
tbsinstall=protecting_path('tbs-install','Protect an alcohol as TBS ether','Ethanol','CCO','TBSCl, imidazole','Ethyl TBS ether','CCO[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C','Alcohol oxygen silicon પર substitution કરે છે. O–H mask થાય છે; carbon framework અને મૂળ C–O bond જળવાય છે.',steps(('Activate / deprotonate','Base proton transfer અને silyl transfer ને facilitate કરે છે.','Alcohol / base lone pair','Silicon / proton'),('Attack silicon','Alcohol oxygen electrophilic Si પર attack કરે છે.','Alcohol O lone pair','Silicon'),('Leave chloride','Silicon substitution chloride departure સાથે silyl ether આપે છે.','Si–Cl bond','Chloride leaving group'),('Check compatibility','TBS ether ordinary base સામે fairly stable પરંતુ fluoride અને suitable acid પ્રત્યે labile છે.','Protected oxygen','Subsequent reaction planning')),'A strong Si–O bond masks alcohol acidity and nucleophilicity.','Relative acid stability is substrate/condition dependent; “acid-stable” is too absolute.')
tbsremove=protecting_path('tbs-remove','Remove TBS with fluoride','Ethyl TBS ether','CCO[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C','TBAF; proton source / work-up','Ethanol','CCO','Fluoride silicon માટે strong affinity ધરાવે છે. Si–F formation સાથે Si–O cleavage alkoxide આપે છે; protonation alcohol release કરે છે.',steps(('Fluoride attack','F⁻ silicon પર attack કરે છે અને hypercoordinate silicon species તરફ જાય છે.','Fluoride lone pair','Silicon'),('Break Si–O','Si–O cleavage oxygen ને alkoxide રૂપે release કરે છે.','Si–O bond pair','Alcohol oxygen'),('Protonate','Alkoxide suitable proton source પરથી H લે છે.','Alkoxide O','Proton'),('Recover the handle','Free OH ફરી oxidation, acylation અથવા substitution માટે ઉપલબ્ધ છે.','O lone pair','Next functional-group reaction')),'Si–F formation provides strong driving force for desilylation.','Fluoride can affect other silyl groups too; this is not automatically site-selective.')
chapter('tbs','TBS/TBDMS alcohol-protecting group છે. Silyl ether installation alcohol ને mask કરે છે; fluoride અથવા suitable acid તેને remove કરી શકે છે.','TBS survives many bases; F⁻ finds Si.','THP is an acetal protecting group removed with aqueous acid rather than a silicon-specific fluoride pathway.',[tbsinstall,tbsremove],'Which bond-forming interaction is central to fluoride deprotection of TBS?','Formation of a strong Si–F bond',['Formation of an N=N bond','A C–Br radical chain','A Pd–aryl coupling'])
thp=protecting_path('thp-install','Alcohol → THP acetal ether','Ethanol','CCO','Dihydropyran, catalytic acid','Ethyl tetrahydropyranyl ether','CCOC1CCCCO1','Acid DHP enol ether ને activate કરીને oxocarbenium-like center બનાવે છે. Alcohol oxygen attack અને proton transfer પછી acetal THP ether આપે છે.',steps(('Protonate DHP','Enol ether protonation oxocarbenium-like electrophile બનાવે છે.','DHP π electrons','Acid proton'),('Alcohol attack','Alcohol O lone pair acetal carbon પર attack કરે છે.','Alcohol O lone pair','Oxocarbenium carbon'),('Deprotonate','Oxygen deprotonation neutral THP ether આપે છે.','Base lone pair','Oxonium O–H'),('Reverse under aqueous acid','Water અને acid acetal hydrolysis દ્વારા free alcohol પાછો આપે છે.','Water O lone pair','Activated acetal carbon')),'Acetal formation is reversible; changing water activity and acidity shifts protection/deprotection.','The new acetal stereocenter can give diastereomeric mixtures with chiral alcohols.')
chapter('thp','THP protection alcohol ને acetal ether માં ફેરવે છે. It is usually base-stable and acid-labile; protecting-group choice માં hydrolysis conditions ખાસ મહત્વની છે.','THP is an acetal: acid + water undo it.','TBS cleavage involves silicon; THP cleavage is acetal hydrolysis.',[thp],'What functional-group type explains THP acid lability?','Acetal',['Aryl fluoride','Unactivated alkane','Tertiary phosphine'])
bocinstall=protecting_path('boc-install','Amine → N-Boc carbamate','Glycine','NCC(=O)O','Boc₂O, appropriate base / medium','N-Boc glycine','CC(C)(C)OC(=O)NCC(=O)O','Amine nitrogen Boc₂O carbonyl પર attack કરે છે. Acyl substitution carbamate આપે છે; glycine ના COOH group ને આ scheme માં esterified માનવામાં આવતો નથી.',acyl_steps('Amine N lone pair','tert-butoxycarbonate-derived fragment'),'Carbamate resonance reduces amine nucleophilicity; leaving carbonate fragments can lose CO₂.','Boc goes on N in this example; it is not the same as making a tert-butyl ester.')
bocremove=protecting_path('boc-remove','Acidic Boc deprotection','N-Boc glycine','CC(C)(C)OC(=O)NCC(=O)O','TFA or HCl; then appropriate isolation','Glycine parent amine','NCC(=O)O','Acid tert-butoxy unit cleavage promote કરે છે. Carbamic-acid-derived intermediate CO₂ ગુમાવી amine આપે છે; acidic solution માં amine often ammonium salt તરીકે રહે છે.',steps(('Protonate carbamate','Acid protonation tert-butyl cleavage facilitate કરે છે.','Carbamate O lone pair','Acid proton'),('Lose tert-butyl fragment','C–O cleavage isobutene/tert-butanol-derived products આપી શકે છે.','tert-Butyl O–C bond','Fragmentation pathway'),('Decarboxylate','Carbamic acid CO₂ lose કરે છે.','Carbamic-acid bond system','Amine + CO₂'),('Read salt state','Acidic medium માં amine protonated હોઈ શકે; drawing neutral parent બતાવે છે.','Amine N lone pair','Proton / isolation state')),'CO₂ loss makes carbamate fragmentation favorable.','Do not confuse acid-labile Boc with base-labile Fmoc.')
chapter('boc','Di-tert-butyl dicarbonate (Boc₂O) amine પર Boc carbamate install કરે છે. Boc group mild base સામે generally stable અને acidથી removable છે; peptide protection માં તેનો ઉપયોગ થાય છે.','Boc: base-tolerant protection, acid removes it.','Fmoc is commonly removed with base; Cbz commonly by hydrogenolysis.',[bocinstall,bocremove],'Which site is protected in the displayed glycine + Boc₂O example?','The amino nitrogen',['The carboxyl carbon becomes silicon','The α-carbon is brominated','Only the carboxylic OH is tert-butylated'])
