fmocremove=protecting_path('fmoc-remove','Base-mediated Fmoc removal','N-Fmoc ethylamine',fmocsm,'Piperidine / DMF','Ethylamine parent','CCN','Base fluorene 9-position પર proton remove કરીને elimination trigger કરે છે. Dibenzofulvene બને છે; carbamate-derived fragment CO₂ ગુમાવી amine release કરે છે.',steps(('Deprotonate fluorene','Fluorenyl proton removal resonance-stabilized anion આપે છે.','Base lone pair','Fluorenyl C–H proton'),('β-Elimination','Dibenzofulvene formation carbamate unit release કરે છે.','Fluorenyl anion / C–O system','Exocyclic alkene'),('CO₂ loss','Carbamate-derived intermediate decarboxylate થઈ amine આપે છે.','Carbamate bond system','CO₂ + amine'),('Trap the byproduct','Piperidine dibenzofulvene સાથે react કરીને removal clean રાખવામાં મદદ કરે છે.','Piperidine N lone pair','Dibenzofulvene electrophile')),'Fluorenyl anion stabilization and elimination explain base sensitivity.','Base-sensitive groups elsewhere can be affected during deprotection.')
chapter('fmoc','Fmoc carbamate acid-tolerant, base-removable amine protection આપે છે. Fluorenyl framework ની special deprotonation/elimination chemistry orthogonality માટે જવાબદાર છે.','Fmoc falls to base; Boc falls to acid.','Both are carbamates, but their cleavable alkoxy groups create different deprotection pathways.',[fmocinstall,fmocremove],'What initiates standard base-mediated Fmoc removal?','Deprotonation at the fluorenyl position followed by elimination',['Hydrogenolysis of every aromatic ring','Direct fluoride attack at silicon','A bromonium-ion opening'])
