cbzremove=protecting_path('cbz-remove','Hydrogenolytic Cbz removal','N-Cbz ethylamine',cbzsm,'H₂, Pd/C','Ethylamine parent','CCN','Hydrogenolysis benzyl–oxygen linkage cleave કરે છે. Carbamic-acid-derived intermediate CO₂ lose કરે છે અને amine release થાય છે; benzyl fragment typically toluene બને છે.',steps(('Adsorb and activate hydrogen','Catalyst H₂ અને benzyl-containing substrate ને activate કરે છે.','H₂ / catalyst surface','Activated hydrogen'),('Hydrogenolyze benzyl linkage','Benzyl–O bond cleavage carbamic-acid-derived unit આપે છે.','Benzylic C–O bond','Hydrogenolysis fragments'),('Decarboxylate','Carbamic acid CO₂ ગુમાવે છે.','Carbamic-acid bond system','Amine + CO₂'),('Check other reducible groups','Alkenes/benzyl groups જેવા hydrogenation-sensitive handles પણ react થઈ શકે છે.','Other reducible functionality','Selectivity decision')),'A hydrogenolytically cleavable benzyl unit distinguishes Cbz from Boc and Fmoc.','Hydrogenation-sensitive groups may be reduced during Cbz removal.')
chapter('cbz','Cbz/Z protection benzyl carbamate બનાવે છે. Mild acid/base હેઠળ often stable હોય છે; hydrogenolysisથી remove કરી શકાય છે.','Cbz has a benzyl handle: H₂/Pd removes it.','Boc cleavage is acid-driven; Fmoc cleavage is base-driven.',[cbzinstall,cbzremove],'Which method is commonly used to remove Cbz?','Hydrogenolysis with H₂/Pd',['PCC oxidation','A Suzuki coupling','Only dry NaOH at room temperature'])

