acoh2=pathway('acoh-alpha','AcOH as medium for α-bromination','Propanone','CC(C)=O','Br₂ / CH₃COOH','Bromoacetone','CC(=O)CBr','Acetic acid medium carbonyl enolization ને support કરે છે. Enol bromine સાથે reaction કરીને α-carbon પર C–Br bond બનાવે છે; bromination સીધી carbonyl carbon પર નથી થતી.',alpha_steps,'The enol is the carbon nucleophile and Br₂ supplies electrophilic bromine.','An unsymmetrical ketone may present regioselectivity questions; acetone is symmetric.','AcOH supplies medium/acid chemistry; Br₂ is the brominating reagent.')
chapter('acetic-acid','Acetic acid solvent, proton donor અથવા acid medium બની શકે છે. Reagent નો role ચોક્કસ substrate અને co-reagents પરથી નક્કી થાય છે; AcOH ને દરેક scheme માં oxidant ન ગણવો.','AcOH sets the medium; look for the real redox reagent.','Acetic anhydride transfers an acetyl group; AcOH in the two reference pathways mainly supports the medium.',[acoh1,acoh2],'What is the principal role of AcOH in Zn/AcOH ozonolysis work-up?','Acidic medium / proton source',['The original alkene-cleaving oxidant','A borohydride source','A palladium ligand'])
anhyd1=pathway('anhyd-alcohol','Alcohol acetylation','Ethanol','CCO','Acetic anhydride; appropriate acid/base catalyst','Ethyl acetate','CCOC(C)=O','Alcohol oxygen acetic anhydride ના electrophilic carbonyl પર attack કરે છે. Tetrahedral intermediate collapse થઈ acetate ester અને acetate/acetic-acid-derived byproduct આપે છે.',acyl_steps('Alcohol oxygen','acetate'),'The alcohol’s original R–O bond remains; a new O–C(O)CH₃ bond is formed.','No stereocenter in ethanol; acylation of an existing chiral alcohol normally preserves its C–O configuration.','This is acyl substitution, not SN2 at the acetyl methyl carbon.')
anhyd2=pathway('anhyd-amine','Amine acetylation','Ethylamine','CCN','Acetic anhydride','N-Ethylethanamide','CCNC(C)=O','Amine N lone pair anhydride carbonyl પર attack કરે છે. Amide formation nitrogen basicity/nucleophilicity ઘટાડે છે કારણ કે lone pair carbonyl સાથે delocalize થાય છે.',acyl_steps('Amine nitrogen','acetate'),'Amide resonance changes the nitrogen’s properties; this is why acylation can protect an amine.','No new stereocenter in this example.','Acetamide derivatives are not ordinary amines with unchanged basicity.')
chapter('acetic-anhydride','Acetic anhydride acetyl-transfer reagent છે. Alcohol થી acetate ester અને amine થી acetamide બને છે; બંનેમાં nucleophilic acyl substitution common છે.','Ac₂O adds acetyl; substrate O or N chooses ester or amide.','AcOH and Ac₂O are not interchangeable labels.',[anhyd1,anhyd2],'What distinguishes alcohol and amine acetylation products?','Alcohol gives an ester; amine gives an amide',['Both always give an alkene','Both always give a ketone','Amine gives an ether and alcohol gives a nitrile'])
