al1=pathway('alcl3-alkyl','Friedel–Crafts alkylation','Benzene','c1ccccc1','Ethyl chloride / AlCl₃','Ethylbenzene','CCc1ccccc1','AlCl₃ Lewis acid C–Cl polarization વધારી alkyl electrophile બનાવવામાં મદદ કરે છે. Benzene electrophilic aromatic substitution કરે છે.',eas_steps,'Aromaticity restoration drives the substitution sequence. Carbocation-like intermediates can rearrange.','Rearrangement and polyalkylation can complicate unsymmetrical examples.','Strongly deactivated rings and Lewis-basic amines are problematic substrates.')
al2=pathway('alcl3-acyl','Friedel–Crafts acylation','Benzene','c1ccccc1','Acetyl chloride / AlCl₃; work-up','Acetophenone','CC(=O)c1ccccc1','Acyl halide/AlCl₃ acylium-like electrophile આપે છે. Ring attack અને deprotonation aryl ketone framework બનાવે છે; ketone–AlCl₃ complex માટે work-up જરૂરી છે.',eas_steps,'The acylium ion is resonance-stabilized and does not undergo the ordinary alkyl-carbocation rearrangements. Product acyl groups deactivate the ring.','No stereocenter in acetophenone.','AlCl₃ can bind strongly to the product; “catalyst” does not mean catalytic amounts suffice in every acylation.')
chapter('alcl3','AlCl₃ electron-pair acceptor Lewis acid છે. Friedel–Crafts માં alkylation અને acylation બંને activate કરે છે, પરંતુ intermediates અને limitations અલગ છે.','AlCl₃ accepts a pair; arene attacks the electrophile.','Alkylation may rearrange/polyalkylate; acylation uses an acylium-like electrophile and deactivates the ring.',[al1,al2],'Which electrophile is characteristic of Friedel–Crafts acylation?','Acylium-like ion',['Enolate ion','Sulfur ylide','Hydride ion'],'https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/16-3-alkylation-and-acylation-of-aromatic-rings-the-friedel-crafts-reaction')
nhred=pathway('nh3-alkyne','Dissolving-metal alkyne reduction','But-2-yne','CC#CC','Li or Na, liquid NH₃; proton donor','(E)-But-2-ene','C/C=C/C','Metal electron આપે છે; NH₃ solvent અને medium મુજબ proton source બની શકે છે. Electron–proton–electron–proton sequence suitable internal alkyne ને trans alkene તરફ લઈ જાય છે.',steps(('Electron transfer','Metal alkyne π* orbital માં electron આપી radical anion બનાવે છે.','Metal electron','Alkyne π* system'),('Proton transfer','Radical-anion intermediate proton source પરથી H લે છે.','Anionic electron density','Proton donor'),('Second electron','Second transfer vinyl-anion-derived intermediate આપે છે.','Metal electron','Vinyl radical center'),('Final protonation','Standard internal-alkyne case માં intermediate geometry અને final protonation મુખ્યત્વે E alkene આપે છે.','Vinyl anion pair','Proton donor')),'Stepwise reduction differs from same-face metal-surface hydrogenation.','Predominantly E for the internal alkyne shown.','NH₃ is not the sole source of reducing electrons.','radical')
nhacyl=pathway('nh3-acyl','Acyl chloride ammonolysis','Acetyl chloride','CC(=O)Cl','NH₃; suitable medium','Acetamide','CC(N)=O','Ammonia nitrogen lone pair acyl carbon પર attack કરે છે. Chloride departure અને proton transfer amide આપે છે; another ammonia equivalent acid neutralize કરી ammonium chloride બનાવી શકે છે.',acyl_steps('Ammonia nitrogen','chloride'),'Acyl chloride is activated toward substitution because chloride is a good leaving group.','No new stereocenter.','The product is a primary amide, not a ketone.')
